          "name": "What is the difference between CPI, CPA, and ROAS in app marketing?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "CPI (Cost Per Install) measures the ad cost to generate one app installation. CPA (Cost Per Action) measures the cost to drive a specific in-app event like registration or purchase. ROAS (Return on Ad Spend) calculates the total revenue generated from paying app users relative to your advertising spend."
