								<p class="kdm-faq-answer"><span class="kdm-ans-badge">Ans</span> Yes. We manage specialized growth campaigns for both Android applications on Google Play Store and iOS applications on Apple App Store, adjusting bidding strategies, ad formats, and compliance requirements for each operating system.</p>
							</div>
						</div>

						<!-- FAQ 6 -->
						<div class="kdm-faq-item">
							<button type="button" class="kdm-faq-header">
								<span class="kdm-faq-question">Q.6. What is the difference between CPI, CPA, and ROAS in app marketing?</span>
								<span class="kdm-faq-icon">+</span>
							</button>
							<div class="kdm-faq-body">
								<p class="kdm-faq-answer"><span class="kdm-ans-badge">Ans</span> CPI (Cost Per Install) measures the ad cost to generate one app installation. CPA (Cost Per Action) measures the cost to drive a specific in-app event like registration or purchase. ROAS (Return on Ad Spend) calculates the total revenue generated from paying app users relative to your advertising spend.</p>
							</div>
						</div>

						<!-- FAQ 7 -->
						<div class="kdm-faq-item">
							<button type="button" class="kdm-faq-header">
								<span class="kdm-faq-question">Q.7. How do you protect against click fraud and fake bot app installs?</span>
